        Hi,=0D=0A=0D=0A    I ported the david dawes' intelfb driver from =
kernel 2.4=0D=0Ato the new api of the kernel 2.6. I also made some change=
s and=0D=0Aimprovements.=0D=0AHere is a simplified changelog :=0D=0A     =
         Fix HW accel and HW cursor on i845G=0D=0A              Add TV-Ou=
t functionality (tested with a ch7011 tv =0D=0A              encoder)=0D=0A=
              Use of agpgart for fb memory reservation=0D=0A             =
 Add mtrr support=0D=0A=0D=0A    The main change is for sure the TV-Out s=
upport. I used the =0D=0Akernel i2c api to cleanly communicate between th=
e intelfb=0D=0Adriver and the tv encoder driver. Now, I've written a driv=
er=0D=0Afor Chrontel CH7011 chips (I think it's usable also for=0D=0A7009=
/7012/7301).=0D=0AOther drivers may be written (for connexant, philips an=
d others)=0D=0Awithout fundamentally changing the current api. Also, othe=
r=0D=0Aframebuffer driver could be extended to support tv-out=0D=0A(rivaf=
b i think) and maybe the api could be extended to=0D=0Asupport DFP too.=0D=
=0A   =0D=0A    I still have some problems which i can't still understand=
 :=0D=0A        - the hw cursor is killed by the native i810 driver of =0D=
=0AXFree86 when i return to the console. I cannot recover from=0D=0Ait an=
d an ugly bitmap is flashing instead of the cursor.=0D=0A        - I can'=
t switch back and forth between monitor and=0D=0Atv. All is ok when i boo=
t on tv (with my bios configured to=0D=0Aoutput=0D=0Aon tv) but not when =
i boot on monitor. The registers seems to be=0D=0Aprogrammed exactly the =
same but i must miss something.=0D=0A=0D=0A    And I'm doing my developme=
nt on a 845, not a 865, so=0D=0Achecks on 830, 85X and 865 are needed.=0D=
=0A    All patches and fixes are welcome :-)=0D=0A=0D=0ASylvain=0D=0A=0D=0A=
